Add a Remote Query producer through the Postgres check's standard optional resolve/execute interface: resolve database_instance and tuple targets inside the check's effective monitoring scope (configured database plus autodiscovery) with a side-effect-free per-check resolve verdict, execute the strictly validated query exactly once in a read-only transaction whose statement timeout the remote_queries.timeout_ms instance option may only shorten, and stream the result as native COPY CSV pages directly to its-agent-intake per page, with array element delimiters resolved from catalog metadata. Producer runs also open native ddtrace producer spans at the producer's phase boundaries through the shared base tracing machinery, fail-open. Unscheduling a check with a remote query in flight now stops the query promptly: the check registers its live remote-query connections for the exact window it holds them and the cancellation thread sends each a protocol-level cancel request (cancel_safe, bounded and privilege-free), the interrupted run reports the sanitized retryable cancelled outcome with its upload aborted and transaction rolled back, and the check's deferred teardown runs only after the query has unwound, so scheduled monitoring queries and the connection pool are never released under a live remote call.
